  "note": "Third remediation revision (findings F1-F9 from an independent static review, validated by a second agent). Applied to BOTH the private bench copy and this portable copy: parser containment and bounded/sanitised diagnostics, the reporter-to-collector null contract, a control-master liveness gate with no interactive fallback, recorded tri-state ownership with durable pending-cleanup evidence, SIGHUP/SIGTERM teardown in both modes, verified master shutdown, explicit boot identity, and reporter output-integrity/format fixes. Only deliberate configuration differences remain (bench target/user, data dir, artifact and known_hosts defaults and pinned digests, and config.example.json). The two trees' collector tests are now byte-identical, so no sanitized test addresses remain. Second follow-up (collector 1.5.2): provisioning facts are read where a failed start() enters the collector, so no classifier branch can drop them; a cancellation during the control-master exit is held for one bounded check, recorded by stage and re-raised. Every hash below was regenerated from the files themselves in that revision: eight portable entries had not been refreshed for 1.5.1 and no longer matched the committed files, and the two follow-up regression suites were not listed. Third follow-up (collector 1.5.3): an absolute data directory and sample pointer, one final-cleanup record per run, a persisted master verdict after a failed provision, and no false persistence error on a cancelled first run. Fourth follow-up (collector 1.5.4): a legacy relative sample pointer resolves inside its owning store and never against the working directory; a directory an established session could not remove is queued for reconciliation by the attempt that learns of it; and the controlling-terminal tests name the runner restriction that makes them fail under a sandbox. Every hash below was regenerated from the files themselves in the 1.5.4 revision: the 1.5.3 revision had not refreshed this manifest, so 4 entries no longer matched the committed files and the third follow-up's regression suite was not listed.",
